"""Create an inspectable problem-discovery brief without model calls."""
import html,json
from pathlib import Path

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
OUT=ROOT/"output"/"problem-selection-brief"
evidence=json.loads((ROOT/"research/problem_selection_evidence.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
study=ROOT/"output/problem-selection-v2-live"
results=json.loads((study/"results.json").read_text()) if (study/"results.json").exists() else None
OUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
esc=lambda s:html.escape(str(s))
css="body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1100px;margin:35px auto;padding:20px;color:#18232c}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{border:1px solid #ccc;padding:10px;vertical-align:top;text-align:left}section{margin:28px 0}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;background:#f5f5f5;padding:16px}summary{cursor:pointer}a{color:#175a9e}.note{border-left:4px solid #b87816;padding:12px;background:#fff8e7}@media print{body{margin:0}details>*{display:block}}"
parts=['<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Problem selection — evidence and next gate</title><style>'+css+'</style>',
       '<h1>Find the problem before choosing the product</h1><p>Research checkpoint · 30 October 2026 · Meta hackathon, Push the Frontier</p>',
       '<p class="note">This brief separates reported user problems, vendor capability claims, and our synthetic feasibility test. It does not establish a new scientific discovery, customer adoption, or manufacturing readiness.</p>',
       '<h2>Decision</h2><p>Prioritize a designer-reviewed revision-checking trial. Do not start a general CAD editor. Keep simulation diagnosis as a second option until a complete reproducible model and intended physical result are available.</p>',
       '<p>The rubric favors impact (30%), Meta use (25%), execution (20%) and demo (25%). Novelty is not a separate criterion. Existing competitors set a baseline; they do not automatically disqualify a useful hackathon implementation.</p>',
       '<h2>Two candidate problems</h2><table><tr><th>Direction</th><th>Evidence and existing workflow</th><th>What could earn a build</th><th>Risk</th></tr>']
for c in evidence['comparison']:
    parts.append('<tr><td>'+esc(c['direction'])+'</td><td>'+esc(c['evidence'])+'<br><br>'+esc(c['existing_tools'])+'</td><td>'+esc(c['possible_Meta_role'])+'<br><br>'+esc(c['decision'])+'</td><td>'+esc(c['risk'])+'</td></tr>')
parts.append('</table><h2>Small real Meta trial</h2>')
if results:
    parts.append('<p>13 constructed revision packets. Text and typed records only: no drawing OCR or native CAD ingestion. A paired continuation sees checker feedback and uses one extra model call. Oracle-form results assume the correct interpretation is manually provided; they are not measured human performance.</p>')
    parts.append('<pre>'+esc(json.dumps({'summary':results['summary'],'provider':results['provider']},indent=2))+'</pre>')
    parts.append('<p><a href="../problem-selection-v2-live/report.html">Inspect every packet, expected requirement, actual model response and check</a> · <a href="../problem-selection-v2-live/protocol.json">Frozen protocol</a> · <a href="../problem-selection-v2-live/api-events.jsonl">Actual request/response ledger</a></p>')
    parts.append('<p class="note"><b>Interpretation:</b> Both Meta modes score 12/13 against frozen exact labels. The only disagreement is R02: ask for approval versus block an unapproved supplier change. All core dimensions, materials and clearance bases match in 13/13. The prompt itself allows flagging unapproved substitutions, so this label difference is debatable; it is not evidence of a dimensional mistake. Both modes withhold clearance. Gold labels remain unchanged. The extra feedback turn did not improve the result. This supports limited language-to-requirement feasibility, not a competitive or customer-value claim.</p><p><a href="../problem-selection-v2-live/independent-audit.json">Independent ledger, context and decimal-arithmetic audit</a></p>')
else:parts.append('<p>Running; no result asserted.</p>')
parts.append('<h2>What would justify a product build?</h2><ol><li>The designer identifies a recurring revision mistake or review burden their current workflow does not already handle adequately.</li><li>One real or faithfully reconstructed revision can be replayed from exported records with accepted expected outcomes.</li><li>A user test compares the existing workflow, a structured form with deterministic checks, and Meta-assisted extraction. Include correction/import effort, not just API time.</li><li>The live demo handles a fresh request and explicitly stops on missing intent. Geometry success never becomes a claim of material/strength qualification.</li></ol>')
parts.append('<p><a href="designer-review.html">Short designer review sheet</a> — prepared for the user; not sent to anyone.</p><h2>Source casebook</h2>')
for s in evidence['sources']:
    title=esc(s['id']+' — '+s['kind'])
    if s['url']:title='<a href="'+esc(s['url'])+'">'+title+'</a>'
    parts.append('<section><b>'+title+'</b><p>'+esc(s['finding'])+'</p></section>')
parts.append('<h2>Reproducibility and provenance</h2><pre>python -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_problem_selection.py -v\npython -m problem_selection.study report --directory output/problem-selection-v2-live\npython research/audit_problem_selection.py\npython research/problem_selection_report.py</pre><p>These commands are offline. A fresh run requires prepare with a new directory followed by run; run makes paid requests. The real-run inputs, expected outputs, protocol and source were frozen before its API calls. The v1 preparation hit a Windows manifest-path bug before any request. The v2 sandbox attempt failed DNS before any model response. Both are retained separately; the unchanged live study then ran with network access. They are not scored inference attempts or concealed model failures.</p><p>All new files are isolated under problem_selection, its test file, research/problem_selection* and research/audit_problem_selection.py, and output/problem-selection*. Earlier experiments and results were not rewritten. Model billing was not independently verified.</p>')
(OUT/'index.html').write_text('\n'.join(parts),encoding='utf-8')
review=['<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Designer review — revision workflow</title><style>'+css+'</style>',
        '<h1>Is this a real problem worth solving?</h1><p>For a product designer working on stalls, crates or comparable static assemblies. No client names or files are needed. These examples are invented and have not been validated by a designer.</p>',
        '<h2>Start with your experience, before the examples</h2><ol><li>Think of your most recent material or dimensional revision. What actually took effort, and what already updated automatically?</li><li>Which mistake, if any, was hardest to notice? Where did the authoritative requirement live?</li><li>How did you check the final model, drawing and BOM? Could a linked property, equation or existing checker have prevented the issue?</li><li>What records could you export without re-entering the design? Would exporting them take longer than checking the change yourself?</li><li>Would you use a reviewer for this, or is this the wrong problem? What would be more useful?</li></ol>',
        '<h2>Three hypothetical cases to critique</h2><ol><li><b>Preserve the opening.</b> A casing is 600 mm outside with 1.2 mm side panels. A change calls for 6 mm panels while preserving the existing usable opening. A proposed 606 mm outside width meets an old 594 mm minimum. Is this kind of wording conflict realistic, or would your CAD/requirement setup eliminate it?</li><li><b>Supplier suggestion versus approval.</b> A supplier suggests thicker plastic panels. The draft model is updated before the customer confirms dimensions/material. Does this happen in your workflow? Who resolves it and how?</li><li><b>Mixed handoff.</b> The CAD is revised but one exported drawing or BOM remains from the earlier revision. Is that a meaningful problem with your actual release process, or does PDM already prevent it?</li></ol>',
        '<h2>Small test we would ask for next</h2><p>Only if one case is relevant: replay one anonymized prior revision or a designer-created representative example. Record the current method, our assisted method, corrections needed and total time including export/import. A useful result could be a saved review step; it does not need to be a novel structure.</p>',
        '<details><summary>Arithmetic for the first example, after giving your opinion</summary><p>Old actual nominal opening: 600 − 2×1.2 = 597.6 mm. New proposal: 606 − 2×6 = 594 mm. Preserving 597.6 mm nominal would require 609.6 mm outside. If 606 mm is locked, the requirements conflict. This is geometry only, not material or strength validation.</p></details>']
(OUT/'designer-review.html').write_text('\n'.join(review),encoding='utf-8')
print(OUT/'index.html')
